# One fresh read-only legacy graph verification

This release candidate checks the saved five-array graphs for ETH2022-01-03
and2022-06-13 sequentially. It never starts the original producer, decodes raw
transactions, samples neighborhoods or fits a model. The original FAILED claim
and all109historical cells remain unchanged. Existing-output verification spends
no additional empirical attempt;33/60spent and27fullyallocated remain unchanged.

Before execution, the independent release review and its acceptance record must
be committed together with exact source-bindings.json. That manifest inherits
the1798byte bindings closed by the corrected named offline verification, adds
all current checker/metadata/wrapper sources and retained tests/reviews, and
binds the31compact metadata files and original preparation. The acceptance
record binds both manifest and review hashes without a self-referential hash.
The requested40hex source must match HEAD; all bound current and committed
bytes must agree. Exact Python3.13.13/NumPy2.3.0 versions are checked. Installed
library byte identity beyond the locked project files is not asserted.

Run only `PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -B <this-directory>/run_verification.py
--source <fresh-reviewed-commit>`. The launcher refuses an existing
verification01 identity or another active replication guard. It durably reserves
verification01 before guard startup; a startup failure keeps that reservation.
No retry is permitted under this identity, including partial or failed startup.
Guard:3GiBmemory.max/2GiBmemory.high/zero swap/two CPUs via existing reviewed
guard implementation,3GiBhostreserve/6GiBstartupreserve/10GiBdiskfloor/1800seconds.
Fresh resource preflight is required before launch; source and HEAD then freeze.

The child reserves exclusive payload receipts, revalidates committed source,
checks its fresh live monitor lease/boot/owner/cgroup/limits, reads only bounded
regular single-link compact files through nonsymlink paths, and validates all
legacy joins before opening an array. Each array verifier receives the exact
manifest hash and declared graph extent, bounded by562,558,280bytes. Explicit
mapping cleanup occurs before moving to the next graph. Guard/compact-input
checks precede and follow each graph; final source is checked again. Any partial
graph receipt remains preserved on later failure. Resource guardian death/limit
failure can interrupt verification and is retained as a failed attempt.

Source/stat checks assume no malicious concurrent filesystem writer. Whole
process memory is enforced by the finite guard, not inferred from array size.
Verification independently checks saved-array hashes, canonical graph identity,
structure, counts and aggregate features. Raw transaction uniqueness, values,
exclusions and provider semantics remain qualified producer evidence. Success
does not admit future graph reuse or prove paper numerical agreement.

Close only after child/guard result, both graph summaries, source/input hashes,
mapping cleanup, exact monitor/child death, absent cgroup and independent review
agree. Preserve every failed attempt; no silent rebuild or replacement.

Component evidence:12tiny synthetic array tests;10compact metadata checks;
7tiny mocked callback/receipt/guard-boundary tests. The corrected metadata
denominator and coverage tests propagate dependent hashes and assert their
specific diagnostics (metadata-green02.log); previous masked tests and review
are retained. Callback tests do not measure empirical arrays or kernel limits.
